<Landing
  title="The Glovebox Is Not a Filing System — CabSnap"
  description="The glovebox keeps the paper but not the writing. Photograph receipts as you get them and the record survives. Free on Google Play."
  path="/lp/glovebox"
  kicker="Free on Google Play"
  headlines={{
    a: "The glovebox is not<br />a <em>filing system</em>.",
    b: "By April it's a<br /><em>paper brick</em>.",
    c: "You mean to sort it.<br />You <em>never</em> sort it.",
  }}
  sub="It holds everything you put in it and loses nothing. It just can't stop thermal paper going blank while it sits there."
>
  <ul class="points">
    <li>Photograph it once, at the pump, in three seconds</li>
    <li>The AI pulls the vendor, date, and total automatically</li>
    <li>Filed and searchable instead of crammed in a compartment</li>
    <li>Keep using the glovebox for the paper if you like</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="para">
    Nothing in there is lost. That is the frustrating part &mdash; the receipts
    are exactly where you left them, and half of them have nothing left to read.
  </p>

  <p class="para">
    Take the photo first. Then the compartment can go back to what it's good
    at, which is holding things you've already dealt with.
  </p>
</Landing>
